      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "<h1 align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/spark.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"22\" height=\"22\"> Oh My Claude</h1>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  English | <a href=\"README.zh.md\">中文</a>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <strong>Claude Code, native inside dsh</strong>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <em>Drive your logged-in Claude Code CLI as a first-class dsh provider: no API key, no extra services, no runtime dependencies.</em>\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-oh-my-claude\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/dsh-oh-my-claude?style=flat&color=cb3837&logo=npm\" alt=\"npm version\" /></a>\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/host-dsh-6c5ce7?style=flat\" alt=\"dsh\" />\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/drives-Claude%20Code%20CLI-d97757?style=flat\" alt=\"Claude Code CLI\" />\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/language-TypeScript-3178c6?style=flat&logo=typescript\" alt=\"TypeScript\" />\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/build-Bun-f472b6?style=flat&logo=bun\" alt=\"Bun\" />\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/runtime%20deps-zero-45cfa0?style=flat\" alt=\"Zero runtime dependencies\" />\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\">\n  <sub>Built with AI assistance, and open to more. Contributions from AI coding agents are welcome; start with <a href=\"https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</sub>\n</p>\n\n---\n\nClaude Code CLI as an LLM provider for [dsh](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/dsh). Every request drives `claude -p` with stream-json in and out, so it uses whatever login, hooks, CLAUDE.md files, MCP servers and rate limits Claude Code already has. No API key needed. The plugin speaks the CLI's own protocol (the one the Agent SDK wraps) directly, so it has no runtime dependencies.\n\n## Tour\n\n<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/shield-menu.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"dsh's access shield in a Claude session: Plan, Ask, Accept edits, Auto, Don't ask and Bypass rows with dsh's own icons\"></p>\n\nThe shield is dsh's own control. In a Claude session its rows become Claude's six permission modes, each labelled with the dsh access level it sets underneath.\n\n<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/panel-tabs.gif\" width=\"640\" alt=\"the Oh My Claude panel switching between its Memory, Rewind, Changes and Asides tabs\"></p>\n\nOne `✻` button beside the composer opens the whole plugin: Memory, Instructions, Skills, Rewind, Changes, MCP, Asides, Diagnostics, Tasks and Tune, plus a Restore tab while the session is still blank.\n\n<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/panel-changes.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"the Changes tab listing the working tree diff with per-file line counts\"> <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/panel-asides.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"the Asides tab with a side question expanded above the tab strip\"> <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/panel-mcp.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"the MCP tab's add-server form, filled with a server name, command and argument list\"></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/cost-row.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"dsh's footer stats row ending with the Claude session cost and cached token count\"></p>\n\nCost and cached token count, two figures dsh cannot compute, join dsh's footer stats row. The pill turns orange once a session passes the spend line you set. The dollar figures are what the turns would cost at API rates; on a Claude subscription you are not billed them.\n\n<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/context-usage.png\" width=\"300\" alt=\"dsh's context ring popover with Claude plan windows and the CLI's own context breakdown\"> <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/phone-panel.png\" width=\"300\" alt=\"the panel as a phone sheet above the composer\"></p>\n\nPlan usage and the CLI's own context breakdown live in dsh's context ring popover. On a phone the panel becomes a sheet.\n\n<p><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/main/docs/media/add-workspace.png\" width=\"640\" alt=\"dsh's Select Workspace Directory dialog with a box dropdown in its footer listing This box and an ssh box\"></p>\n\nOnce an SSH box is saved, dsh's own Add workspace dialog gains a box dropdown: a folder on that box becomes a workspace here, and the session in it runs Claude Code there.\n\n<sub>Shots by <code>tools/playwright/tour.ts</code>.</sub>\n\n## Install\n\nYou need the Claude Code CLI on `PATH` and logged in (`claude --version` works, `claude` opens without asking you to sign in), and dsh 0.2 (0.2.2-alpha.2 or newer). On dsh 0.2.0 or 0.2.1, install 1.5.14 (`dsh-oh-my-claude@dsh-0.2.1`); on dsh 0.1.x, install the npm tag for your line from the Compatibility table below. Nothing else: no API key, no Node build step.\n\n**From dsh's Plugins page**, in the web app or DSH Desktop:\n\n1. Open **Plugins** in the sidebar and press **Add plugin**.\n2. Enter `dsh-oh-my-claude` and press **Install**.\n3. Press **Enable now**, or turn on its switch later under **Installed plugins**.\n\nIt loads without a restart. Reload the page and \"Oh My Claude\" appears in the model picker with the models your login can use. Pick one and chat.\n\n**From a terminal**, then restart dsh however you run it:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-oh-my-claude\nsystemctl --user restart dsh-web.service\n```\n\nTo install straight from the repository instead of npm, use `github:lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude` as the package name in either route.\n\nThe plugin speaks English and Chinese and follows dsh's own language setting (Settings → General → Language), switching as soon as you change it.\n\nIf the picker lists it as `Oh My Claude (not logged in)`, run `claude auth login` in a terminal on the box that runs dsh, or press Log in under Settings → Oh My Claude → Boxes.\n\n**DSH Desktop** (macOS and Windows) uses the Plugins page steps above. The plugin looks for `claude` in the usual install folders, since an app started from the Dock does not see your shell's PATH. On Windows it runs Claude as a plain child of dsh, so restarting the app ends a running turn, and the parts that need a Unix shell (Log in from Settings, SSH boxes) are not available. The server half has run under Electron on Linux the way Desktop runs it, and on Windows 11 with Claude Code installed from npm.\n\nWhen a newer version is on npm, an orange pill with the version number appears in Settings and on the panel's Runtime line. A click opens Oh My Claude on dsh's Plugins page, where dsh's own Update button installs it; the copy button beside the pill puts the update command on the clipboard for a terminal. DSH Desktop gets the pill too, without the copy button, since its CLI has no command to copy. Details, and the repairs the plugin makes on its own after a dsh upgrade, are under [Plugin updates](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#plugin-updates).\n\nOptional, in `~/.dsh/settings.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nagent-default-model:            # make Claude Code the default for new sessions\n  provider: claude-code\n  model: claude-fable-5-1       # any model id the picker lists\nsubagent-model-selection:       # let dsh subagents run on Claude Code too\n  enabled: true\n  allowedModels:\n    - provider: claude-code\n      model: claude-haiku-5-5   # any model id the picker lists\n```\n\nWorking on the plugin itself? Start at [docs/developing.md](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/developing.md).\n\n## Compatibility\n\ndsh ships prereleases only and moves client APIs between them, so every release of the plugin records the dsh line it was written for and the dsh it was driven on. \"Runs on\" is the range the code carries branches for; \"tested on\" is the dsh installed on the box when the release was cut. The update pill reads the floor off the registry: a box whose dsh is below it is never offered the update command, and the pill names the dsh that release needs instead.\n\n| Plugin | Runs on dsh | Tested on dsh | npm tag |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1.6.3 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 through 0.2.2-rc.2 | 0.2.2-rc.2 | `latest` |\n| 1.6.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | none, superseded by 1.6.3 |\n| 1.6.1 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | none, superseded by 1.6.2 |\n| 1.6.0 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | none, superseded by 1.6.1 |\n| 1.5.14 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | `dsh-0.2.1`, `dsh-0.2` |\n| 1.5.13 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-rc.1 | 0.2.2-rc.1 | none, superseded by 1.5.14 |\n| 1.5.12 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-alpha.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.13 |\n| 1.5.11 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-alpha.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.12 |\n| 1.5.10 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.2-alpha.2 | 0.2.2-alpha.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.11 |\n| 1.5.9 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.4 | 0.2.1-rc.4 | none, superseded by 1.5.10 |\n| 1.5.8 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.4 | 0.2.1-rc.4 | none, superseded by 1.5.9 |\n| 1.5.7 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.3 | 0.2.1-rc.3 | none, superseded by 1.5.8 |\n| 1.5.6 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.3 | 0.2.1-rc.3 | none, superseded by 1.5.7 |\n| 1.5.5 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.2 | 0.2.1-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.6 |\n| 1.5.4 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-rc.2 | 0.2.1-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.5 |\n| 1.5.3 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.1-alpha.1 | 0.2.1-alpha.1 | none, superseded by 1.5.4 |\n| 1.5.2 | 0.2.0-rc.1 through 0.2.0-rc.2 | 0.2.0-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1.5.3 |\n| 1.4.2 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.7-rc.2 | 0.1.7-rc.2 | `dsh-0.1.7` |\n| 1.4.1 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.7-rc.2 | 0.1.7-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1.4.2 |\n| 1.4.0 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.7-rc.2 | 0.1.7-rc.2 | none, superseded by 1.4.1 |\n| 1.3.1 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.6-alpha.2 | 0.1.6-alpha.2 | `dsh-0.1.6` |\n| 1.2.1 | 0.1.5-rc.1 through 0.1.6-alpha.2 | 0.1.6-alpha.2 | `dsh-0.1.5` |\n\n## What you get\n\n1. Any Claude model your login can use, in dsh's own picker. Hide the ones you don't use with a switch in Settings, or with `hiddenModels` in the plugin config. Add one the lineup doesn't list, such as a name your local router sends to another model, in the same Settings block or with `customModels`. The menu follows the router: switch one such as CC Switch on and it lists the router's models, switch it off and Claude's are back, with no reload. An ssh box follows its own router, not this PC's. [Models](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#models)\n2. Every dsh session resumes its Claude Code session, tool history included, and a terminal `claude /resume` sees the same one. [Sessions](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#sessions)\n3. Restart dsh without killing a running Claude turn. [Restarts](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#restarts)\n4. dsh's access shield sets Claude's six permission modes per session. [Permission mode](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#permission-mode-per-session)\n5. Claude's permission prompts, questions and plan reviews become dsh dialogs, each option's preview under the question. [Approvals](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#approvals-and-questions)\n6. One spark button opens Memory, Rewind, Changes, MCP and seven more tabs, all reachable from the keyboard. [The panel](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md)\n7. Cost and cached tokens in dsh's footer, with a spend line that turns the pill orange. [Cost pill](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#cost-pill)\n8. Plan usage (5-hour, weekly, extra usage) in dsh's context ring, which turns amber near a limit and red at one, with a notice above the composer. Only limits the session's model counts against, graded by Anthropic, so a new model needs no update. [Plan usage](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#plan-usage)\n9. Restore or import any past Claude transcript, from dsh or from a terminal, and search inside them for what was said. [Session browser](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#session-browser)\n10. Claude's slash commands and skills show up in dsh's slash menu under their own names, as `/claude-<name>` where dsh already uses the name. A skill dsh also serves runs on any model, and so does one only Claude Code has: typed in a session on another model, it goes to that model with its instructions (switch it off in Settings). [Command bridge](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#command-bridge)\n11. Claude gets dsh's subagents, jobs, goals and web search over MCP. It can also open a new dsh session, send it follow-ups and read its replies (`open_session`, `prompt_session`, `wait_session`). [dsh tools over MCP](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#dsh-tools-over-mcp)\n12. Edit CLAUDE.md, settings.json and MCP servers from the panel, on this box or a remote one, and sign in to an MCP server that needs it. [Instructions](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#instructions), [settings.json editor](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#settingsjson-editor), [MCP](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#mcp)\n13. Run Claude on another box over SSH, or mount several accounts. [Remote boxes and accounts](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/remote.md)\n14. Report a problem with a redacted box report, copied or filed as an issue. [Report a problem](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#report-a-problem)\n15. All the orange is a switch, per group, any colour. [Claude look](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#claude-look)\n16. Pick what dsh adds to your prompts, with the size of each block on the label. [dsh context](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#dsh-context)\n17. A card offers each new Claude Code release for the box a session runs on, and installs it from dsh; a headless `claude -p` never updates itself. Channel, auto-install and history per box sit under the switch in Settings. [Claude Code updates](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#surviving-claude-code-updates)\n18. What the last five versions changed, read from the plugin's own changelog, in Settings. [Changelog](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#changelog)\n19. Every skill the CLI can reach, grouped by scope, with add, edit and remove for your own and the project's. What each costs, from the CLI's own `/skill-doctor`, is a table you can sort, beside what else drives your usage: the MCP servers behind the most requests, and how the work was shaped. [Skills](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#skills)\n20. A mark on the browser tab and an optional desktop notice when a session you are not looking at finishes, or stops to ask you something. [Session notices](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#session-notices)\n21. dsh's own goal and every earlier goal of the session, beside Claude Code's goal and its scheduled tasks. [Tasks](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#tasks)\n22. Edit or remove a message you steered in while Claude works, or all of them as one, until Claude reads it. A file or image on the message stays on it; only the text changes. Nothing goes out while you edit. Send now stops Claude and sends one as the next turn. [Steering](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#dsh-tools-over-mcp)\n23. Claude's working line (spinner, verb, figures) repeats above the composer once you scroll up past it, so reading back through a long turn never hides what Claude is doing. A switch in Settings turns it off. [Turn status](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#turn-status)\n24. Select text in a reply and dsh's popover (dsh 0.2.2) shows Ask beside its Quote text, or on a phone a row above the composer does: ask Claude about the passage as a side question that leaves the conversation alone; ask with the question blank and Claude explains the passage. [Asides](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#asides)\n25. A finished turn keeps a closing line where the working verb was, the way the terminal ends one: `✻ Crunched for 27s · done 3:21 AM`. A turn you stopped reads `Interrupted · What should Claude do instead?`. [Turn status](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#turn-status)\n26. Claude's tool calls show as dsh's own tool cards, the way every other provider's do, with the text streaming between them. Inline text is a switch away in Settings (\"Native tool rows\"). [Native tool rows](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#native-tool-rows)\n27. A new session in a workspace opens on the Claude box, model and effort that workspace last ran, and a workspace with nothing remembered opens on a default model and effort you pick. [Remember model per workspace](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#remember-model-per-workspace)\n28. After each reply, Claude's guess at your next prompt shows above the composer: Use writes it into the box, Send sends it as it is, and it folds away while you type something else. On by default, as in the terminal; a switch in Settings turns it off. [Suggested next prompt](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#suggested-next-prompt)\n29. Claude's background shell tasks and subagents are listed on the Tasks tab while they run, each with Stop and, for a shell task, Output, plus Stop all once two or more run. A shell task that ended keeps its row and its Output for the last ten; the subagents a session already ran sit under Earlier subagents, each openable as Markdown. A subagent's row in the chat names each step as the CLI reports it. [Tasks](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#tasks)\n30. If an `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in dsh's environment is what Claude Code bills instead of your login, the session says so in one line at its start. [Where things live](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#where-things-live)\n31. Each plan window says where it is heading at the current rate: the percent it ends at, or when the cap lands. [Plan usage](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#plan-usage)\n32. Once the context window is 75% full (adjustable in Settings), a card above the composer says so and offers Compact, which sends Claude's own `/compact`. [Context nudge](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#context-nudge)\n33. A Run button on every shell snippet Claude writes puts it in the composer as a prompt; Enter sends it, and it runs through Claude's Bash tool and dsh's approval. [Run a snippet](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#run-a-snippet)\n34. A session renamed in dsh keeps that name in `claude --resume`, and a name set on the Claude side renames the dsh session. [Command bridge](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#command-bridge)\n35. Switch a session between Claude and another model, such as DeepSeek or a local one, and back: Claude sees the prompts, replies and tool use the other model had in between. [Sessions](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#sessions)\n36. Up in an empty composer brings back your last prompt, Up again older ones, Down newer ones and back to empty, as in the Claude Code terminal; typing a character ends the walk. A new session recalls from the workspace's latest transcript. Switch it off under Settings (\"Prompt recall\").\n37. Ctrl+R in the composer searches the prompts typed before: this session, the workspace or everywhere on the box (Ctrl+S or Ctrl+Up/Down cycles). Enter sends the row, Tab writes it into the composer, Esc closes. Switch it off under Settings (\"History search\").\n38. Esc Esc in an empty composer while nothing runs opens the Rewind tab on the latest prompt, as the terminal's double Escape opens /rewind; after the rewind that prompt is back in the composer to edit and resend. Switch it off under Settings (\"Edit last prompt\"). The three composer gestures are listed in dsh's Keyboard shortcuts dialog too.\n39. Three commands of the plugin's own: `/btw <question>` asks Claude a side question without adding to the conversation, `/temporary` keeps no Claude transcript for the session, and `/ultracode` turns Claude Code's ultracode on or off without a relaunch. [Asides](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/panel.md#asides), [Temporary sessions](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#temporary-sessions), [Ultracode](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md#ultracode)\n\nDefaults you never have to touch, such as secret redaction in tool results and surviving the CLI's own updates, are on [How it works](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md).\n\n## Configure\n\nSettings come in two kinds. The switches under Settings → Oh My Claude and in the panel's Tune tab are saved at once and kept on the box, so every browser sees the same ones. A Tune row reaches Claude when its process next starts. The keys below are install-time: they go as `config:` on the bundle row in the profile's `cordis.patch.yml` and take effect when dsh next loads the plugin, which a dsh restart does. dsh's own Plugins page lists the plugin with an on/off switch but has no form for these keys. Three keys people change first:\n\n```yaml\npermissionMode: dsh      # follow the session's shield (default), or pin one of the CLI's six modes\n# spawn: node            # unset: the Settings switch below decides; node or dsh here wins\nsshHost: \"\"              # \"[user@]host\" drives a claude on another machine over ssh\n```\n\nEvery key, with its default, is in [docs/configuration.md](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/configuration.md).\n\n### Keep Claude running across dsh restarts\n\nThis switch under Settings → Oh My Claude picks how Claude Code is started, and it is on unless you turn it off. `spawn: node` or `spawn: dsh` in the config overrides it and locks the switch; `spawn: keeper` leaves it free. A flip reaches each session on its next turn.\n\n| | On (`keeper`) | Off (`dsh`) | `node` (config only) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A turn running when dsh restarts | Keeps running; the new dsh reattaches and shows what it did | Ends; about ten seconds after the restart the session gets a \"dsh restarted while this turn was in progress\" prompt and carries on | Same as off |\n| Left running after dsh exits | Claude, until it has gone `processIdleMs` (30 min, never under 5 min) with no dsh attached and no output | Nothing after a normal shutdown: dsh ends Claude and everything it started | Claude ends when dsh does; what it started is not tracked |\n| dsh's environment | Passed whole | Passed whole except `DSH_*` names: dsh's seam drops names with KEY, TOKEN, SECRET or PASSWORD, and the plugin passes them back | Passed whole |\n| SSH boxes and remote workspaces | The far `claude` is held on the box and survives too; the idle limit above does not reach it, so it runs until a dsh reattaches or the box restarts | The far `claude` ends with the ssh connection | Same as off |\n| Platforms | Linux and macOS; Windows runs `node` | All; `node` when dsh mounts no subprocess seam | All |\n\nDSH Web and DSH Desktop run separate dsh profiles, so each reattaches only to the Claude processes it started. Two dsh started on the same profile directory still share them.\n\n## Remote boxes and accounts\n\nMount the plugin twice with different `configDir` values for two logins. List other boxes running dsh and this plugin under Settings → Oh My Claude → Boxes and jump between them. Or give a box a name and `user@host` and drive the `claude` there over SSH, with nothing on the far side but the CLI; Tailscale and WireGuard peers appear as hosts to pick from. All of it is on [docs/remote.md](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/blob/main/docs/remote.md).\n\n## What it touches\n\n- **Runs** the `claude` binary you already have, on this box or on one you add over SSH.\n- **Reads** Claude Code's login (`~/.claude/.credentials.json`, on macOS the `Claude Code-credentials` Keychain entry when that file has no live token, or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` when set) to fetch the model list and your plan usage. That token goes only to `api.anthropic.com`.\n- **Writes** its own state under `~/.local/state/dsh-oh-my-claude/`; login tokens for SSH boxes are files only you can read. CLAUDE.md, settings.json and MCP servers change only when you edit them from the panel.\n- **Listens** on a Unix socket for the keeper that holds Claude across a dsh restart. Its HTTP routes live inside dsh's own server, so on DSH Web it opens no TCP port. Under DSH Desktop, whose web server answers 403 to anything but its own window, the bridge that hands dsh's tools to Claude also listens on 127.0.0.1, behind the same key.\n- **Calls out** to `api.anthropic.com` (models, plan usage), `status.anthropic.com`, `downloads.claude.ai` (the CLI's release pointer), `registry.npmjs.org` (plugin update check) and `api.github.com` (the repo's star count). SSH goes only to boxes you add.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- dsh's shell and file tools are not proxied (except `bash` for background jobs); Claude Code uses its own, under its own permission mode.\n- Claude Code sessions are not deleted when dsh sessions are.\n\n## Bugs and feedback\n\nFound a bug, or something that reads wrong? Open an issue at [github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/issues](https://github.com/lcestou/dsh-oh-my-claude/issues) with the dsh and Claude Code versions (`dsh --version`, `claude --version`) and what you expected to see. Settings → Oh My Claude → Report a problem writes that report for you.\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](LICENSE).\n\nClaude, Claude Code and the Claude spark mark are trademarks of Anthropic, PBC. This project is an independent dsh plugin that drives the Claude Code CLI you already have; it is not made, endorsed or supported by Anthropic. The spark is drawn here only to say which sessions and controls belong to Claude Code, in the way the CLI itself draws it.\n"
